{
  "id": "breadcrumbs",
  "name": "Breadcrumbs",
  "category": "navigation",
  "description": "The path from the section root down to the record on screen. The last crumb says where you are and is not a link.",
  "when_to_use": "Any page two or more levels deep. One level deep does not need a trail — it needs a back link, which is the back variant here. A page that is a step in a sequence or a panel over another page is not a location at all, and the sequence variant is what that looks like.",
  "rules": [
    "The separator is a slash, always. There is no chevron variant and no icon variant; a trail that reads \"Home / Procurement / PO-24-1187\" in one file and uses chevrons in another is two components pretending to be one.",
    "The last crumb is plain text with aria-current=\"page\". Making it a link to itself is a dead control, and users click it and get nothing.",
    "Never truncate the last crumb. It is the one that says where you are. Truncate the middle, or collapse it into an overflow menu.",
    "The trail is the information hierarchy, not the browsing history. It does not change based on how the user arrived, so two people on the same record see the same trail.",
    "Where a record has more than one plausible parent — a GRN reachable from the order, from the vendor and from the receipt register — the trail takes the one parent that is the same for everybody and the other routes are written beside it as relationships. A crumb chosen from the referrer is history again, and it is the worst kind: it looks like structure, so it is believed.",
    "A crumb the user may not open is named and not linked. Dropping the level makes the trail claim a depth the record does not have; leaving the link in ships a path whose third step is a 403. The same shape covers a parent that was deleted — the stored label, no href, and one line saying why. Where the label itself is what the permission protects, the crumb reads \"Restricted\" instead of the name, because naming it leaks exactly the thing that was locked.",
    "Only the levels the route already proves get a placeholder while the record is fetched. A GRN URL proves there is a register above it and a section above that, so those two can wait as bars. Nothing proves how many levels sit above a search result, and guessing draws a trail that is a different length when it lands.",
    "A step in a sequence is not a level, and neither is a dialog. Steps are not addressable, they hold unsaved input, and a crumb promises a page that can be bookmarked and reloaded. The trail on a wizard names the page the wizard is; the step count sits with the title.",
    "Crumbs are not underlined, unlike every other link in the system. Five underlined links in a row is a fence, not a path; the muted colour and the hover carry it instead."
  ],
  "anatomy": [
    {
      "part": "Trail",
      "description": "A <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"> holding an ordered list, because the order is the information and a screen reader needs to be able to skip it."
    },
    {
      "part": "Crumb",
      "description": "A link to an ancestor page, text-zinc-600, darkening to zinc-900 on hover."
    },
    {
      "part": "Separator",
      "description": "A zinc-500 slash. Decorative and aria-hidden, so it is never read aloud. zinc-400 is the on-dark step of the text scale and is a shade too light for a mark on white."
    },
    {
      "part": "Current crumb",
      "description": "Plain text in zinc-900 font-medium, never a link, carrying aria-current=\"page\"."
    },
    {
      "part": "Overflow",
      "description": "The collapsed middle of a long trail: an ellipsis button and, behind it, a nested ordered list of the levels it hides."
    },
    {
      "part": "Placeholder crumb",
      "description": "An h-2.5 bg-zinc-200 bar in a one-line box, standing where a label will land that the fetch has not returned yet. Not a link, and aria-hidden, so nothing tabs into a grey rectangle."
    },
    {
      "part": "Locked crumb",
      "description": "A level that exists in the hierarchy but not for this user: the label in zinc-500 behind a lock icon, no href, and the reason written on the page under the trail."
    },
    {
      "part": "Relationship line",
      "description": "The other records this one belongs to, under the trail and labelled — ordinary underlined links, so nothing there is mistaken for a level."
    },
    {
      "part": "Trailing controls",
      "description": "Anything that belongs to the record rather than the page — a status pill, a copy-id button. They sit outside the <ol> entirely, beside the nav, never inside the last <li>."
    }
  ],
  "behaviour": [
    "The last crumb is the current page and is not a link. A link to the page you are on is a dead control.",
    "The last crumb is never truncated or collapsed — it is the one that says where you are.",
    "A long trail collapses its middle into an overflow menu rather than wrapping onto two lines.",
    "Below sm the trail collapses to the parent and the current page. Four crumbs at 390px either wrap or push the page sideways, and both are worse than showing two.",
    "The trail reflects the hierarchy, not the history, so it does not change based on how the user arrived.",
    "Crumb labels match the titles of the pages they point at, so following one is not a surprise.",
    "While the parents are in flight, everything the page already knows is drawn for real — the root, and the record number that came out of the URL. Only the labels that are actually waiting are bars, and the trail reflows when they land while the title under it does not move.",
    "A crumb with no href is inert to the pointer and to the keyboard. It does not hover, it does not focus, and it is not a tab stop, because there is nowhere for it to go.",
    "When the page content is swapped without a page load, the trail is swapped with it. A trail left behind by an htmx swap is wrong and silent about it, which is worse than a trail that is missing."
  ],
  "accessibility": [
    "A <nav> with aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\", so assistive technology can identify it and skip past it.",
    "An ordered list inside, because the sequence carries the meaning.",
    "Separators are aria-hidden, or a screen reader reads \"slash\" between every crumb.",
    "The current page carries aria-current=\"page\" — that, not the styling, is what announces it.",
    "The overflow button has an aria-label naming how many levels it hides, because an ellipsis says nothing on its own.",
    "The overflow panel is a list of links and carries no role=\"menu\". role=\"menu\" promises the menu keyboard model — arrows between items, Home and End, one tab stop for the set — and a panel of plain anchors delivers none of it. Links in a list are already navigable; take the role and the browser stops treating them as links.",
    "Crumb links declare the same focus outline as every other control in the system: focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15. The trail is often the first thing under the skip link, so it is the first place a keyboard lands on a record page, and leaving it to the user agent means the indicator changes between browsers on the one control that is guaranteed to be reached by keyboard.",
    "While the trail is loading, aria-busy sits on the <nav> and the placeholder crumbs are aria-hidden, with one sr-only role=\"status\" naming the record outside them. Read out, a bar is an empty list item, and three of them is a trail that appears to have lost its labels.",
    "A crumb that is not a link says so in text — an sr-only clause after the label — rather than in the lock icon, which is aria-hidden, or in the grey, which is not announced at all."
  ],
  "related": [
    "page-header",
    "tabs",
    "sidebar",
    "skeleton"
  ],
  "variants": [
    {
      "id": "default",
      "name": "Default",
      "html": "<!-- Three levels, which is the common case. The separator is aria-hidden so a\n     screen reader reads \"Home, Procurement, Purchase orders\" rather than\n     spelling out a slash between each one.\n\n     The focus outline is declared on the crumbs rather than left to the\n     browser. On a record page the trail is usually the first thing after the\n     skip link, so it is the first thing a keyboard reaches, and it is the one\n     control on the page guaranteed to be tabbed through. -->\n<nav data-kui=\"breadcrumbs/default\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n  <ol class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-[13px]/5\">\n    <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Home</a></li>\n    <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n    <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Procurement</a></li>\n    <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n    <li><span aria-current=\"page\" class=\"font-medium text-zinc-900\">Purchase orders</span></li>\n  </ol>\n</nav>"
    },
    {
      "id": "record",
      "name": "On a record",
      "html": "<!-- A record page. The status and the copy button belong to the record, not to\n     the trail, so they sit outside the <ol> entirely — one flex row holding the\n     nav and then the controls.\n\n     Inside the last <li> they would be read as part of the fourth list item:\n     \"PO-24-1187 Awaiting GRN Copy order number\" announced as one crumb, in an\n     ordered list whose last entry is now a control. Outside it, the list has\n     four crumbs and the pill is a sibling of the trail, which is what it is.\n\n     The pill is badge's locked shape, copied class for class — graphite, and\n     the state lives in the 6px dot. A trail is not the place to invent a second\n     status treatment. -->\n<div data-kui=\"breadcrumbs/record\" class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2.5 gap-y-1.5\">\n  <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n    <ol class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-[13px]/5\">\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Home</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Procurement</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Purchase orders</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><span aria-current=\"page\" class=\"font-medium tabular-nums text-zinc-900\">PO-24-1187</span></li>\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n\n  <span class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-zinc-200 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-[12px]/4 font-medium text-zinc-700 ring-1 ring-inset ring-zinc-300\">\n    <span class=\"size-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>Awaiting GRN\n  </span>\n\n  <button type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Copy order number\"\n          class=\"inline-flex size-7 items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-zinc-600 hover:bg-zinc-200 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">\n    <i data-lucide=\"copy\" class=\"size-3.5\"></i>\n  </button>\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "truncated",
      "name": "Long labels",
      "html": "<!-- Vendor and project names run long. The middle crumbs truncate; the last one\n     never does. min-w-0 on the <li> is what makes truncate work at all inside a\n     flex row — without it the item refuses to shrink below its content.\n\n     title is a fallback, not the fix. It never appears on a touch device and it\n     cannot be reached by keyboard, so the full label has to exist somewhere\n     else on the page as well — as the h1, or as the record line under it. What\n     title buys is the mouse user checking which of two rate contracts this is\n     without leaving the page. -->\n<nav data-kui=\"breadcrumbs/truncated\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n  <ol class=\"flex flex-nowrap items-center gap-1.5 text-[13px]/5\">\n    <li class=\"shrink-0\"><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Home</a></li>\n    <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"shrink-0 text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n    <li class=\"min-w-0 max-w-[14ch] shrink\">\n      <a href=\"#\" title=\"Procurement &amp; stores\" class=\"block truncate text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Procurement &amp; stores</a>\n    </li>\n    <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"shrink-0 text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n    <li class=\"min-w-0 max-w-[18ch] shrink\">\n      <a href=\"#\" title=\"Gujarat Polymers Ltd — annual rate contract\" class=\"block truncate text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Gujarat Polymers Ltd — annual rate contract</a>\n    </li>\n    <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"shrink-0 text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n    <li class=\"shrink-0\"><span aria-current=\"page\" class=\"font-medium tabular-nums text-zinc-900\">PO-24-1187</span></li>\n  </ol>\n</nav>"
    },
    {
      "id": "overflow",
      "name": "Collapsed middle",
      "html": "<!-- Past four levels the middle collapses behind an ellipsis rather than\n     wrapping onto a second line. The button says how many levels it hides,\n     because an ellipsis on its own announces nothing.\n\n     The hidden levels are a nested <ol> inside the <li> they collapsed from,\n     not a menu. They are still crumbs and they are still in order, so the outer\n     list reads as four items with three nested inside the second — which is the\n     truth — and every one of them is an ordinary link the browser already knows\n     how to move between. role=\"menu\" here would promise arrow keys, Home and\n     End and a single tab stop for the set, and this panel implements none of\n     that; taking the role also stops the items being announced as links, which\n     is the one thing they certainly are.\n\n     The panel takes max-w-[calc(100vw-2rem)] because at 390px a fixed w-60\n     anchored to a crumb halfway along the trail hangs off the right edge and\n     pushes the page sideways.\n\n     @click.stop on the button and the panel keeps the document-level handler\n     from closing this menu the moment it opens. -->\n<nav data-kui=\"breadcrumbs/overflow\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" x-data=\"{ open: false }\" @click.outside=\"open = false\" @keydown.escape.window=\"open = false\">\n  <ol class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-[13px]/5\">\n    <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Home</a></li>\n    <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n    <li class=\"relative\">\n      <button type=\"button\" @click.stop=\"open = !open\"\n              aria-label=\"Show 3 hidden levels\" :aria-expanded=\"open\"\n              class=\"rounded-md px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-600 hover:bg-zinc-200 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">…</button>\n      <ol x-show=\"open\" x-cloak @click.stop\n          class=\"absolute top-full left-0 z-40 mt-1 w-60 max-w-[calc(100vw-2rem)] overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-zinc-300 bg-white py-1 shadow-lg\">\n        <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"block truncate px-3 py-2 text-[13px]/5 hover:bg-zinc-100 focus-visible:bg-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:-outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700\">Procurement</a></li>\n        <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"block truncate px-3 py-2 text-[13px]/5 hover:bg-zinc-100 focus-visible:bg-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:-outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700\">Purchase orders</a></li>\n        <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"block truncate px-3 py-2 text-[13px]/5 hover:bg-zinc-100 focus-visible:bg-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:-outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700\">Gujarat Polymers Ltd</a></li>\n      </ol>\n    </li>\n    <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n    <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"tabular-nums text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">PO-24-1187</a></li>\n    <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n    <li><span aria-current=\"page\" class=\"font-medium text-zinc-900\">Line 4 — MS angle 50×50×6</span></li>\n  </ol>\n</nav>"
    },
    {
      "id": "loading",
      "name": "The parents are still loading",
      "html": "<!-- A deep link straight to a receipt. The URL carries the record and nothing\n     else: which order it was raised against, and therefore which vendor sits\n     above it, is not known until the record comes back.\n\n     Two of the four crumbs are drawn for real through the wait, and they are\n     the two the page already has. The root is a constant. GRN-26-0418 came out\n     of the URL and is already the h1 under this trail, so greying it out would\n     flash away the one fact the page can state and land it again a moment\n     later.\n\n     Bars stand only where the route proves a level exists. A receipt URL proves\n     there is a register above it and a section above that, so those two can\n     wait as bars. Nothing proves the depth above a search result or a\n     cross-linked record, and a guessed placeholder draws a trail that is a\n     different length when it resolves.\n\n     The bar reserves the line, not the width — no label width is knowable in\n     advance, so the crumbs to its right do move when the labels land. What must\n     not move is anything below: the row is one line tall now and one line tall\n     afterwards, so the h1 and the record card under it stay where they are.\n\n     animate-pulse sits on each bar rather than on a wrapper around the list,\n     because real crumbs are interleaved with the placeholders and neither the\n     root nor the record number has any business pulsing. Both bars start in the\n     same paint, so they stay in phase. aria-hidden moves down onto the <li> for\n     the same reason, and the sr-only status sits outside them, or it would be\n     hidden along with the thing it is announcing. -->\n<nav data-kui=\"breadcrumbs/loading\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" aria-busy=\"true\">\n  <span class=\"sr-only\" role=\"status\">Loading the trail for GRN-26-0418</span>\n  <ol class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-[13px]/5\">\n    <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Home</a></li>\n    <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n    <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"flex h-5 items-center\">\n      <span class=\"h-2.5 w-20 animate-pulse rounded bg-zinc-200 motion-reduce:animate-none\"></span>\n    </li>\n    <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n    <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"flex h-5 items-center\">\n      <span class=\"h-2.5 w-32 animate-pulse rounded bg-zinc-200 motion-reduce:animate-none\"></span>\n    </li>\n    <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n    <li><span aria-current=\"page\" class=\"font-medium tabular-nums text-zinc-900\">GRN-26-0418</span></li>\n  </ol>\n</nav>"
    },
    {
      "id": "restricted",
      "name": "A level you cannot open",
      "html": "<!-- A rate contract hangs off exactly one vendor, so the vendor is a level and\n     not a relationship. The stores user reading this contract for its prices\n     has no access to the vendor master at all: the level is real and the page\n     behind it is closed to them.\n\n     Three ways to draw this and two of them are wrong. Dropping the level makes\n     the trail claim a depth the record does not have, so somebody counts three\n     crumbs and concludes the contract belongs to the register rather than to a\n     vendor. Leaving the link in ships a path whose third step is a 403, which\n     is a trap the user can only find by falling into it. What is left is the\n     label with no href: the hierarchy stays honest and nothing on screen offers\n     to take you somewhere you cannot go.\n\n     A parent that was deleted takes this exact shape — the label the record\n     stored, no href, one line saying what happened. Only the reason differs.\n\n     The reason is a line on the page rather than a title attribute. title never\n     appears on a touch device and cannot be reached by keyboard, so a trail\n     that explains itself only on hover explains itself to about half the people\n     who need it.\n\n     The lock is aria-hidden and the grey is not announced at all, so the fact\n     that this crumb is not a link is carried by an sr-only clause on the label.\n     A crumb that is silently inert reads to a screen reader as a crumb whose\n     link the page forgot.\n\n     Where the label is itself what the permission protects — a customer name on\n     a costing branch, a salary band — the crumb reads \"Restricted\" and nothing\n     more. Naming it in the trail leaks the thing the lock was for. -->\n<div data-kui=\"breadcrumbs/restricted\">\n  <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n    <ol class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-[13px]/5\">\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Home</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Rate contracts</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5\">\n        <i data-lucide=\"lock\" class=\"size-3.5 text-zinc-500\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>\n        <span class=\"text-zinc-500\">Gujarat Polymers Ltd<span class=\"sr-only\">, not available to you</span></span>\n      </li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><span aria-current=\"page\" class=\"font-medium tabular-nums text-zinc-900\">RC-24-0089</span></li>\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n  <p class=\"mt-1.5 text-[12px]/4 text-zinc-500\">Vendor records are open to purchase and finance. The contract is yours to read; the vendor page behind it is not.</p>\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "ambiguous",
      "name": "When the parent is a choice",
      "html": "<!-- One receipt, three plausible parents. Stores reached it from the receipt\n     register, purchase reached it from PO-24-1187, and accounts reached it from\n     the vendor. Each of those is a real relationship and none of them is the\n     hierarchy.\n\n     So the trail stops at the level that is the same for everybody — the\n     register the record lives in — and the relationships are written under it,\n     labelled, as ordinary links. A short honest trail beats a long one whose\n     third crumb depends on the referrer: that crumb is browsing history wearing\n     a hierarchy's clothes, and because it looks like structure it is believed.\n     Two people compare notes on the same GRN and read different paths to it.\n\n     The tempting alternative is to make the middle crumb a picker of the three\n     parents. It is a control that changes what the page above it claims to be\n     while the page itself does not change, and the first thing a user does with\n     it is assume the record moved.\n\n     Every link on that line is named by what the relationship is — order,\n     vendor, store — and all three are underlined, unlike the crumbs. Between\n     the label and the underline there is nothing left to mistake: what is in\n     the <ol> is a level, what is under it is a related record, and a bare row\n     of three links with no labels would read as the trail continuing. -->\n<div data-kui=\"breadcrumbs/ambiguous\">\n  <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n    <ol class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-[13px]/5\">\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Home</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Stores</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Goods receipt</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><span aria-current=\"page\" class=\"font-medium tabular-nums text-zinc-900\">GRN-26-0418</span></li>\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n\n  <p class=\"mt-1.5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-[12px]/4 text-zinc-600\">\n    <span class=\"text-zinc-500\">Order</span>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"tabular-nums text-zinc-900 underline underline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">PO-24-1187</a>\n    <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">·</span>\n    <span class=\"text-zinc-500\">Vendor</span>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-900 underline underline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Sharma Steel &amp; Alloys</a>\n    <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">·</span>\n    <span class=\"text-zinc-500\">Store</span>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-900 underline underline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Silvassa</a>\n  </p>\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "responsive",
      "name": "On a phone",
      "html": "<!-- The same trail twice, and only one is ever visible. Below sm everything\n     between the root and the parent is dropped and the parent takes a back\n     chevron, because four crumbs at 390px either wrap onto two lines or push\n     the page sideways.\n\n     The chevron sits inside the anchor, not beside it in the <li>. Outside it,\n     it is a 14px graphic that looks like the control and is not part of it, so\n     the one press on the page that most needs a thumb-sized target is the text\n     alone.\n\n     Both copies sit in the DOM, and that is safe here only because hidden and\n     sm:hidden compile to display:none, which takes the inactive one out of the\n     accessibility tree as well as off the screen. Hide one with opacity or\n     visibility instead and a screen reader reads the path twice, and the\n     landmark list grows a second nav called Breadcrumb. -->\n<div data-kui=\"breadcrumbs/responsive\">\n  <!-- phone: parent and current only -->\n  <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"sm:hidden\">\n    <ol class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[13px]/5\">\n      <li class=\"shrink-0\">\n        <a href=\"#\" class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1 py-1 text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">\n          <i data-lucide=\"chevron-left\" class=\"size-3.5\"></i>Purchase orders\n        </a>\n      </li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li class=\"min-w-0\"><span aria-current=\"page\" class=\"block truncate font-medium tabular-nums text-zinc-900\">PO-24-1187</span></li>\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n\n  <!-- sm and up: the full trail -->\n  <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"hidden sm:block\">\n    <ol class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-[13px]/5\">\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Home</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Procurement</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Purchase orders</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><span aria-current=\"page\" class=\"font-medium tabular-nums text-zinc-900\">PO-24-1187</span></li>\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "page-header",
      "name": "Above a page title",
      "html": "<!-- Where a trail actually lives. It sits above the title, not beside it, and\n     the title repeats the last crumb — that repetition is correct: the crumb is\n     navigation and the h1 is the page.\n\n     Render it here only if the topbar does not carry one. One of the two,\n     decided once for the whole application; on screen twice, the second one is\n     the one that goes stale.\n\n     Both buttons are h-8, not padding-sized. A pair of controls that take their\n     height from py-1.5 on a 13px line measure 32px, which is not one of the\n     three button heights, and the mismatch shows the moment one of them sits\n     next to a control that is. -->\n<div data-kui=\"breadcrumbs/page-header\" class=\"rounded-xl border border-zinc-300 bg-white px-5 py-4\">\n  <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n    <ol class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-[13px]/5\">\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Home</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Procurement</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><span aria-current=\"page\" class=\"font-medium tabular-nums text-zinc-900\">PO-24-1187</span></li>\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n\n  <div class=\"mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3\">\n    <div>\n      <h1 class=\"text-[20px]/7 font-semibold tracking-tight tabular-nums\">PO-24-1187</h1>\n      <p class=\"mt-0.5 text-[13px]/5 tabular-nums text-zinc-600\">Gujarat Polymers Ltd · raised 14 Aug 2026 · 6 lines · ₹12,45,000</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"flex shrink-0 items-center gap-2\">\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"inline-flex h-8 items-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 bg-white px-3 text-[13px]/5 font-medium hover:bg-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Export</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"inline-flex h-8 items-center rounded-lg bg-zinc-700 px-3 text-[13px]/5 font-medium text-white hover:bg-zinc-800 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Approve</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "sequence",
      "name": "Steps are not levels",
      "html": "<!-- A four-step create screen. The trail has four crumbs and none of them is a\n     step.\n\n     A crumb promises a page: a URL you can bookmark, reload and send to\n     somebody. A wizard step is none of those things. It is a state in a form\n     holding input nobody has saved yet, so a crumb reading \"Lines and rates\"\n     offers to navigate to something that does not exist, and the press either\n     does nothing or throws away work. Draw the steps as steps — that is\n     progress, and it is the component that owns them — and let the trail say\n     the only thing that is true about location here: this is the new-order page\n     under Purchase orders.\n\n     A dialog is the same argument one step further. It is not a location at\n     all, so nothing in the trail moves while it is open: the page underneath is\n     still where the user is, and the dialog says what it is in its own title.\n     A trail that grows a crumb when a modal opens has to lose it again on\n     cancel, and for the length of that modal the address bar and the trail\n     disagree.\n\n     \"New order\" is the current crumb and it is not a link, exactly as on any\n     other page. The step count sits with the h1, in tabular figures so it does\n     not jitter between step 2 and step 3. -->\n<div data-kui=\"breadcrumbs/sequence\" class=\"rounded-xl border border-zinc-300 bg-white px-5 py-4\">\n  <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n    <ol class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-[13px]/5\">\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Home</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Procurement</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Purchase orders</a></li>\n      <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n      <li><span aria-current=\"page\" class=\"font-medium text-zinc-900\">New order</span></li>\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n\n  <div class=\"mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1\">\n    <h1 class=\"text-[20px]/7 font-semibold tracking-tight\">New purchase order</h1>\n    <p class=\"text-[13px]/5 text-zinc-600\"><span class=\"tabular-nums\">Step 2 of 4</span> · Lines and rates</p>\n  </div>\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "back",
      "name": "One level deep",
      "html": "<!-- Not a breadcrumb, and that is the point. One level deep there is nothing to\n     trace, so a trail of two is ceremony. A back link says the same thing in\n     less space and gives a bigger target on a phone.\n\n     It names the place it goes to. \"Back\" on its own is the browser button\n     wearing a page's clothes: it points at history, so it lands somewhere\n     different depending on how the user arrived, which is the one thing this\n     component exists not to do. -->\n<a data-kui=\"breadcrumbs/back\" href=\"#\" class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 py-1 text-[13px]/5 text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">\n  <i data-lucide=\"chevron-left\" class=\"size-4\"></i>Purchase orders\n</a>"
    },
    {
      "id": "htmx",
      "name": "The trail follows the swap",
      "html": "<!-- A receipt queue where opening a row swaps the pane instead of loading a\n     page. The trail sits outside that swap, so unless something moves it, it\n     goes on naming the record the user opened first. A trail that is wrong is\n     worse than a trail that is missing: nothing about it looks stale.\n\n     So the response carries the trail back out of band. The pane markup is the\n     body of the reply and the nav is addressed by id alongside it:\n\n       <nav id=\"bc-trail\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" hx-swap-oob=\"true\"> … </nav>\n\n     The server renders it because the server is the only side that knows the\n     hierarchy. Rebuilding the trail in the browser out of the row that was\n     clicked is history again, and it produces a different path for the same\n     record depending on which queue somebody came through.\n\n     hx-push-url is what keeps the address bar honest, and it is also the test\n     of the whole arrangement: paste the pushed URL into a new tab and the\n     server has to render this page, this pane and this trail with no htmx\n     involved. If it cannot, the trail was a client-side fiction.\n\n     Every row is a real anchor with a real href, so the queue still works with\n     a middle click, with a bookmark, and with JavaScript off.\n\n     The trail is not a live region. Walking a queue of forty receipts would\n     announce four crumbs on every arrow key, over the top of the pane the user\n     is trying to hear. What is announced is the record, so the pane heading\n     carries tabindex=\"-1\" and takes focus after the swap — the moving of that\n     focus is list-detail's job and not this component's. -->\n<div data-kui=\"breadcrumbs/htmx\" class=\"overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-zinc-300 bg-white\">\n  <div class=\"border-b border-zinc-200 px-4 py-3\">\n    <nav id=\"bc-trail\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n      <ol class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-[13px]/5\">\n        <li><a href=\"/\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Home</a></li>\n        <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n        <li><a href=\"/stores/\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Stores</a></li>\n        <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n        <li><a href=\"/stores/grn/\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">Goods receipt</a></li>\n        <li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>\n        <li><span aria-current=\"page\" class=\"font-medium tabular-nums text-zinc-900\">GRN-26-0418</span></li>\n      </ol>\n    </nav>\n  </div>\n\n  <ul class=\"divide-y divide-zinc-100 border-b border-zinc-200\">\n    <li>\n      <a href=\"/stores/grn/26-0418/\"\n         hx-get=\"/stores/grn/26-0418/pane/\" hx-target=\"#bc-pane\" hx-swap=\"innerHTML\"\n         hx-push-url=\"/stores/grn/26-0418/\"\n         class=\"flex items-center justify-between gap-3 bg-zinc-100 px-4 py-2.5 text-[13px]/5 hover:bg-zinc-200 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:-outline-offset-3 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">\n        <span class=\"truncate font-medium tabular-nums\">GRN-26-0418</span>\n        <span class=\"shrink-0 tabular-nums text-zinc-500\">18 Aug 2026</span>\n      </a>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <a href=\"/stores/grn/26-0419/\"\n         hx-get=\"/stores/grn/26-0419/pane/\" hx-target=\"#bc-pane\" hx-swap=\"innerHTML\"\n         hx-push-url=\"/stores/grn/26-0419/\"\n         class=\"flex items-center justify-between gap-3 px-4 py-2.5 text-[13px]/5 hover:bg-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:-outline-offset-3 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">\n        <span class=\"truncate tabular-nums\">GRN-26-0419</span>\n        <span class=\"shrink-0 tabular-nums text-zinc-500\">19 Aug 2026</span>\n      </a>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <a href=\"/stores/grn/26-0420/\"\n         hx-get=\"/stores/grn/26-0420/pane/\" hx-target=\"#bc-pane\" hx-swap=\"innerHTML\"\n         hx-push-url=\"/stores/grn/26-0420/\"\n         class=\"flex items-center justify-between gap-3 px-4 py-2.5 text-[13px]/5 hover:bg-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:-outline-offset-3 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">\n        <span class=\"truncate tabular-nums\">GRN-26-0420</span>\n        <span class=\"shrink-0 tabular-nums text-zinc-500\">19 Aug 2026</span>\n      </a>\n    </li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <div id=\"bc-pane\" class=\"px-4 py-3\">\n    <h2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"text-[16px]/6 font-semibold tracking-tight tabular-nums\">GRN-26-0418</h2>\n    <p class=\"mt-0.5 text-[13px]/5 tabular-nums text-zinc-600\">Sharma Steel &amp; Alloys · 9 lines · 24.500 MT received at Silvassa</p>\n  </div>\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "django",
      "name": "Django template",
      "html": "<!-- The trail comes from the view as a list of (label, url) pairs, with the\n     last entry carrying no url. forloop.last is what decides which crumb is\n     plain text, so the template never has to be told twice where it is.\n\n     # views.py\n     context['crumbs'] = [\n         ('Home', reverse('home')),\n         ('Procurement', reverse('procurement:index')),\n         ('Purchase orders', reverse('po:list')),\n         (order.number, None),\n     ]\n\n     Build it in the view, not in the template. A trail assembled from\n     request.path is browsing history wearing a hierarchy's clothes.\n\n     A pair whose url is None renders as text wherever it falls, not only at the\n     end, which is what a level the user may not open looks like coming out of a\n     get_queryset that filtered it: the label is still known to the record, the\n     link is not there to be followed, and the loop needs no third case. -->\n<nav data-kui=\"breadcrumbs/django\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n  <ol class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-[13px]/5\">\n    {% for label, url in crumbs %}\n      {% if not forloop.first %}<li aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-zinc-500\">/</li>{% endif %}\n      <li>\n        {% if forloop.last %}\n          <span aria-current=\"page\" class=\"font-medium tabular-nums text-zinc-900\">{{ label }}</span>\n        {% elif url %}\n          <a href=\"{{ url }}\" class=\"text-zinc-600 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15\">{{ label }}</a>\n        {% else %}\n          <span class=\"text-zinc-500\">{{ label }}<span class=\"sr-only\">, not available to you</span></span>\n        {% endif %}\n      </li>\n    {% endfor %}\n  </ol>\n</nav>"
    }
  ]
}
